keep-data: the old system Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm) (old.example.net) on /dev/mapper/vg0-root; UEFI firmware; the layout of the profile is not applied, no disk is wiped or partitioned
FORMAT (what is on them is lost)
  /dev/mapper/vg0-root  ext4   /  (10G)
  /dev/vda2             ext4   /boot  (1G)
  /dev/vda4             ext4   /srv/plain  (8G, label plain)
KEEP (as they are, mounted where they were)
  /dev/vda1             vfat   /boot/efi  (the EFI system partition: not formatted, the new boot loader is added)
  /dev/mapper/vg0-swap  swap   swap
  /dev/mapper/vg0-data  xfs    /data
  tmpfs                 tmpfs  /tmp
  /var.old/exports/pub  none   /srv/pub
  /srv/plain/site       none   /srv/www
  /opt/app              none   /srv/app
ASIDE (kept, under another name)
  /dev/mapper/vg0-var   ext4   /var -> /var.old  (mounted)
LOST (on the old root, beyond the system itself)
  /backup  2M
  /etc  6M
  /home/alice  1.1G
  /home/bob  1M
  /opt  245M
  /root  1M
  /usr/local  69M
  /var/lib/apt  176M
  /var/lib/docker  8.5G
WARNINGS
  the source /srv/plain/site of the bind mount at /srv/www was on a volume that is formatted: the new system gets an empty directory there, so that the mount does not fail
  the source /opt/app of the bind mount at /srv/app was on the old root: the new system gets an empty directory there, so that the mount does not fail
  /var/exports/pub of the entry at /srv/pub is on a volume that is set aside: the entry names /var.old/exports/pub from now on
--- /etc/fstab
# /etc/fstab, written by UMP (keep-data: the root made anew, the old system's other volumes as they were)
UUID=NEW-vg0-root  /  ext4  defaults,errors=remount-ro  0 1
UUID=NEW-vda2  /boot  ext4  defaults  0 2
UUID=769B-CE7F  /boot/efi  vfat  umask=0077  0 1
/dev/mapper/vg0-swap  none  swap  sw  0 0
/dev/mapper/vg0-var  /var.old  ext4  defaults  0 2
/dev/vg0/data  /data  xfs  defaults,noatime  0 2
LABEL=plain  /srv/plain  ext4  defaults  0 2
tmpfs  /tmp  tmpfs  nosuid,nodev,size=1G  0 0
/var.old/exports/pub  /srv/pub  none  bind  0 0
/srv/plain/site  /srv/www  none  bind  0 0
/opt/app  /srv/app  none  bind  0 0
